
# Day 42: Maximum Depth of a Binary Tree

## Problem
Find the maximum depth of a binary tree.

## Approach
1. If the root is None, return 0.
2. Calculate the left subtree depth recursively.
3. Calculate the right subtree depth recursively.
4. Return 1 plus the larger depth.

## Example
The longest path is 1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 5.

## Output
Maximum depth: 4

## Time Complexity
O(n), where n is the number of nodes.

## Space Complexity
O(h), where h is the height of the tree, due to recursion.

## Key Learning
The maximum depth is one plus the maximum depth of the left and right subtrees.
